# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion SHIP gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-2 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the approved commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-2/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# B0 (STOP): build the SHIP image from the commit that records the owner's approval, with c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic baked as the image's
# serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as its max-num-seqs (8). REFUSED by c2_serving_job.read_bake and by build-c2-serving-image.sh
# while the profile's owner_traffic_waiver (id w2-er-fx-262k-2026-10-11) has a decision that does not start with APPROVED: the owner approves first, the approval is
# committed (make_fusion_profiles.py --approve-ship), the CPU suite runs on that commit, and the tag is pushed on THAT commit (docs/tp4-ship-ln-w2-er.md,
# docs/tp4-fusion.md). READ: 'baking the serving default c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic with a session cap of 8', the provenance report '(c) the
# image default is the BAKED profile ...', no problem line, the image id. A build with the fusion levers' files in the overlay: the overlay manifest is the one image list.
# Measured basis: the tp4-ship-1 build took 35 minutes. Duration (estimate): 35 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-2
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic
